[s0l0!-header][h1]Queue in Python[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

Let's implement the [b]Queue[/b] class with it's corresponding [b]enqueue[/b], [b]dequeue[/b], [b]is_empty [/b]and [b]print[/b] methods.

We will use a [b]list[/b] to store the elements. [code format="py" codeId="1282"]class Queue:
  def __init__(self):
    self.items = []

  def [b]is_empty[/b](self):
    return self.items == []

  def [b]enqueue[/b](self, item):
    self.items.insert(0, item)

  def [b]dequeue[/b](self):
    return self.items.pop()

  def [b]print_queue[/b](self):
    print(self.items)[/code]
The [b]enqueue[/b] method adds an element at the beginning of the list, while the [b]dequeue[/b] method removes the last element.
